1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
Hi, if you're like me, you spent hours scrolling on TikTok or Pinterest looking at Minecraft

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:07,720
building ideas without the intent to ever actually build them.

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:12,600
Now, I don't know about you, but sometimes inspiration just randomly hits.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,360
And I have to play Minecraft.

5
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,960
Like that's all that's on my mind.

6
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:19,760
And lately I've been seeing a whole lot of cottagecore Minecraft content circulating

7
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:22,900
around the internet, getting a lot of views.

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:27,799
And so I downloaded some shaders and launched Minecraft at like 6 FPS and built this for

9
00:00:27,799 --> 00:00:29,440
nostalgia.

10
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:33,080
And if you're like literally any person who's played Minecraft over the years, these houses

11
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,939
were the bomb.

12
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:37,099
They were like move-in ready.

13
00:00:37,099 --> 00:00:40,900
Of course, there was only room for like three things to fit in there.

14
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,060
And then there was this problem.

15
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:46,779
It's Minecraft cottagecore aesthetic because the mushroom houses with this aesthetic are

16
00:00:46,779 --> 00:00:48,220
like next level.

17
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,220
They are chef's kiss.

18
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,779
They are immaculate.

19
00:00:50,779 --> 00:00:55,820
And suddenly your wiki how tutorial on how to make simple mushroom houses featuring acacia

20
00:00:55,820 --> 00:01:01,060
plank flooring are more an aesthetic than the 2013 mustache trend.

21
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:09,019
And if this strangely specific scenario applies to you, then boy will you like this tutorial.

22
00:01:09,019 --> 00:01:14,820
So now I present three ways to make mushroom houses in Minecraft.

23
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:17,239
Yay.

24
00:01:17,239 --> 00:01:19,900
So the first house is pretty easy.

25
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:24,139
You're going to want to start out with a statistically impossible mushroom in the middle of a field

26
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:26,139
and use bone meal to make it big.

27
00:01:26,139 --> 00:01:31,620
Now stare at that mushroom until you decide to mutilate it to look aesthetic like this.

28
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:35,580
I wanted the mushroom to look a bit different than the other simple mushroom houses you

29
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:41,900
typically see, so I went for a more of a bell shaped curve for the top of the mushroom.

30
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:45,500
You could also use one of those mini water bottles for reference.

31
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:51,139
I modeled mine based on an upside down flower pot and I think it turned out pretty good.

32
00:01:51,139 --> 00:01:56,260
Once you have achieved maximum upside down flower pot conformity, then you can start

33
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:59,339
modifying the stem to make it look stalkier.

34
00:01:59,339 --> 00:02:04,440
I used the mushroom stem block and smooth quartz stairs, and if you're in survival you'll

35
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:08,419
probably want to mine a few of the big mushrooms with a silk touch axe to get the materials

36
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:09,419
for this.

37
00:02:09,419 --> 00:02:13,160
I used birch plank flooring to match the rest of the interior.

38
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:16,020
Now I really like this house, but there's not mushroom.

39
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:18,979
Sorry for my spore sense of humor.

40
00:02:18,979 --> 00:02:22,020
Here's the big grand reveal of this house.

41
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:26,020
Very simple, I give it a 8 out of 10.

42
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,020
Next house!

43
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:30,300
This is a little bit more difficult than the last one, and so you're going to start out

44
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:34,860
by making a frame that looks like the outline of a handmade cube of playdough, the kind

45
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:38,919
that the edges never seem sharp enough, and then start sculpting it to look like the body

46
00:02:38,919 --> 00:02:43,500
of this absurdly priced plastic mini mouse teapot I found on Amazon.

47
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:49,220
I used smooth quartz blocks, slabs, and stairs to accomplish this, and if you want to use

48
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:53,380
mushroom stem blocks, I'm sure you could, but I just like quartz because it makes the

49
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:57,720
mushroom stems seem smooth and continuous, sort of like a differentiable equation.

50
00:02:57,720 --> 00:03:01,080
Also because it's not a pain to get all those stems.

51
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:05,059
After this, start making the stem taller to look almost like a BB-8, and then give the

52
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:07,699
wannabe BB-8 some helicopter blades.

53
00:03:07,699 --> 00:03:10,979
These will be the radius of your circular mushroom cap.

54
00:03:10,979 --> 00:03:14,179
Then connect those little helicopter blades to form a circle.

55
00:03:14,179 --> 00:03:20,100
Also, I never really found these graphs useful, I always find them on like TikTok, but then

56
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,580
again I always just wing it, and it doesn't look very circular, so maybe they're helpful

57
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:26,300
to you, but mine turned out pretty great in the end.

58
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:31,380
Anyway, start outlining the circle in red mushroom blocks, and then be indecisive, and

59
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:36,259
then decide on making the easy way out, and make a circular, spherical looking mushroom

60
00:03:36,259 --> 00:03:37,699
cap.

61
00:03:37,699 --> 00:03:40,979
Mine is about 6 blocks tall, and unlike me, you probably want to make sure there's no

62
00:03:40,979 --> 00:03:42,699
weird blocks left exposed.

63
00:03:42,699 --> 00:03:47,740
Then, I made the door and the window and outlined them in the most superior wood type, spruce

64
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:48,740
wood.

65
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:52,460
I used planks, fences, and stairs as well as oak leaves for the window boxes.

66
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:56,779
To add some extra whimsy, you can make a dilapidated cobblestone chimney and drape that with oak

67
00:03:56,779 --> 00:03:57,779
leaves.

68
00:03:57,779 --> 00:04:04,460
To add some stuff to the interior, I connected the chimney to a fireplace furnace type thing,

69
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:08,820
and then added an unnecessary amount of bookshelves and leaves, because when in doubt, add oak

70
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:11,300
leaves and bookshelves, that's my motto.

71
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:15,899
Also, I used flowerpots, turtle eggs, and sea pickles for the inside, and then I discovered

72
00:04:15,899 --> 00:04:21,019
that in 1.16.5, you can place turtle eggs on flowerpots, which is kind of weird.

73
00:04:21,019 --> 00:04:25,899
Anywho, I used vines as a ladder to the attic area, which will be a cute little bedroom.

74
00:04:25,899 --> 00:04:30,260
I outlined the roof with spruce wood, and then placed some bookshelves behind them.

75
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:34,140
This would also be a cool enchanting room, but the house demands a bedroom, so I added

76
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:38,260
in a skylight, which looks good with the shaders, and I'm sure it would look good without them.

77
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,459
So this is the finished build.

78
00:04:39,459 --> 00:04:44,500
It only took me about 45 minutes to do in creative, so not too bad.

79
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,500
Ta-da!

80
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:50,019
Alright, on to the last one!

81
00:04:50,019 --> 00:04:54,540
This one is kinda hard, but not like PryorGaming at the end of his TikToks kinda hard.

82
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:58,540
You're gonna wanna start out with a circular base like such, and then add a small circle

83
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:00,019
attached to it.

84
00:05:00,019 --> 00:05:03,579
Once you have your two little circle buddies, start making them taller and rounder.

85
00:05:03,579 --> 00:05:07,380
I focused on the bigger circle first, because it's going to be the centerpiece for the build.

86
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:11,299
Also, if this video gets 100 likes, I'll make a video of my little sister following this

87
00:05:11,299 --> 00:05:14,940
tutorial to see how she does, because she's bad at building and I'm bad at explaining

88
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:15,940
things.

89
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,140
Okay, back to the tutorial.

90
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:20,260
If you don't know what shape to make the base of the big mushroom, I referred to the gourd

91
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:25,420
from the 2007 Disney classic, Secret of the Magic Gourd, and mine turned out pretty alright.

92
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:29,619
Also, I need to know, was anyone else low-key traumatized by that movie?

93
00:05:29,619 --> 00:05:33,339
Cause when I first saw that movie, I guess I just thought gourds were strange pumpkins,

94
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:38,500
so for the longest time, I was fundamentally confused on what gourds were.

95
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:42,019
So anyway, you're gonna start making another one of those helicopter circle things, and

96
00:05:42,019 --> 00:05:46,859
here's a better explanation using calculus if you wanna know how to make circles in Minecraft.

97
00:05:46,859 --> 00:05:48,899
Presenting, building circles, yay!

98
00:05:48,899 --> 00:05:53,059
So you're gonna wanna start out with this sort of graph paper, just trace something

99
00:05:53,059 --> 00:05:57,619
circular onto it, and then fill in the blocks that the circle crosses.

100
00:05:57,619 --> 00:05:59,299
Make sure it all has the same radius.

101
00:05:59,299 --> 00:06:00,619
And then this is where the calculus comes in.

102
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:04,940
If you look at tangent lines, you know what tangent lines are, I hope.

103
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:06,899
You probably don't.

104
00:06:06,899 --> 00:06:11,299
But the slope of the tangent line is sort of the slope of if you were to draw the slope

105
00:06:11,299 --> 00:06:15,200
through the, like, the grid squares of the circle.

106
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:20,799
This made a lot more sense inside my head, but you can trace pretty much any circle onto

107
00:06:20,799 --> 00:06:24,540
graph paper and repeat this process, just make sure the radius is the same and that

108
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:26,299
each quadrant is the same.

109
00:06:26,299 --> 00:06:29,140
And there you go, you have a circle in Minecraft!

110
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:34,500
Okay, now moving on to our other little mushroom buddy, you're gonna wanna make him a wonky

111
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:37,299
little mushroom that sort of stems off from the big one.

112
00:06:37,299 --> 00:06:40,980
It's really hard to explain how I did this, but I would recommend using organic shapes

113
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,920
and have the top of the mushroom thinner than the base.

114
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,220
Then add a tiny little cap.

115
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:49,140
For the top of the big mushroom, I basically did the same thing as I did for the medium

116
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:53,679
tutorial, and despite it being vastly bigger, the cap is about the same height.

117
00:06:53,679 --> 00:06:55,700
Maybe even 5 blocks this time.

118
00:06:55,700 --> 00:07:00,380
I kinda wanted to make it sort of sushi-like the first build, but I lost all my brain cells

119
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:02,380
thinking about calculus.

120
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,779
If you want the mushroom to be super cottagecore, you can add some birch leaves that hang like

121
00:07:05,779 --> 00:07:07,980
vines and some hanging lanterns.

122
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,859
You could also use shroom lights.

123
00:07:09,859 --> 00:07:13,660
I also added a dilapidated chimney to match the vibe.

124
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:17,420
And then for the interior, I started again by connecting the fireplace to the chimney

125
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:20,420
and built a loft area with a ladder leading up to it.

126
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:25,100
And then I got distracted by a wandering trader and quickly resumed my work.

127
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:28,619
And I used an absurd amount of birch leaves to decorate.

128
00:07:28,619 --> 00:07:31,739
If you can't tell from my Pinterest page, birch leaves are my favorite.

129
00:07:31,739 --> 00:07:35,579
Also, if you're wondering how they move in the wind, that's the shaders, and I use

130
00:07:35,579 --> 00:07:36,859
BSL shaders.

131
00:07:36,859 --> 00:07:39,540
As far as I know, they only work for Java Edition.

132
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:43,339
I made a little kitchen space in front of one of the windows, complete with some cake

133
00:07:43,339 --> 00:07:46,980
and some turtle eggs, and then added some seating by the fire.

134
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:50,980
In front of the other window, I made what HGTV calls a breakfast nook, complete with

135
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,260
some plants.

136
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:55,820
While the bedroom space is smaller than the previous build, I think it turned out nicely

137
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:57,779
and I wouldn't mind living there.

138
00:07:57,779 --> 00:08:01,700
After decorating the bedroom, I remembered there was a bunch of empty space in the loft

139
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:05,779
which I promptly decorated with barrels because that can be practical when they're not converting

140
00:08:05,779 --> 00:08:07,500
all the villagers to fishers.

141
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:11,940
And I did notice I accidentally made a sort of shrine to Pinocchio, which is cool I guess.

142
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:17,420
On the outside, I was going for a house-ish entrance, but I ended up making it more like

143
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:20,540
a hobbit hole with spruce trapdoors and slabs and stairs.

144
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:26,380
I also added some dark oak for better contrast, and ended up expanding the windows downward

145
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,540
because it just looked better.

146
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:32,500
I added some shutters to the bedroom window and shroom lights to better illuminate it

147
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:33,979
at night.

148
00:08:33,979 --> 00:08:37,219
There was something that was still missing though, and I couldn't decide what to do,

149
00:08:37,219 --> 00:08:41,580
so I tried this thing I saw on TikTok where you make mushrooms out of end rods and mushroom

150
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:46,500
blocks, which I was a bit skeptical of, but I really liked how they turned out.

151
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:51,859
So yeah, those are three mushroom houses you could easily build in Minecraft.

152
00:08:51,859 --> 00:08:56,020
Comment below which one you'd live in, I know I definitely would pick the second one because

153
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:58,500
of the skylight, but that's just me.

154
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:03,419
And if you enjoy this content and would like to see more dollar store green tutorials,

155
00:09:03,419 --> 00:09:05,900
please feel free to hit subscribe.

156
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:07,179
See y'all later, bye!


